WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:01.416
(yelling)

00:00:01.416 --> 00:00:03.127
- I'm in a hood softball league.

00:00:03.127 --> 00:00:06.302
We done had people from
numerous backgrounds that did

00:00:06.302 --> 00:00:07.552
negative stuff.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.615
Guys that sit up there
and rob, people that

00:00:11.615 --> 00:00:13.794
sit up there and sell dope.

00:00:13.794 --> 00:00:16.819
- Well, they went to prison;
they went to jail, but when

00:00:16.819 --> 00:00:20.402
we started this league,
they came together.

00:00:21.431 --> 00:00:24.953
The purpose of this league
was to bring all The Crips

00:00:24.953 --> 00:00:28.425
together and be a family. Well,
if it wasn't this softball

00:00:28.425 --> 00:00:31.633
league I would've never met Tree.

00:00:31.633 --> 00:00:34.216
(upbeat music)

00:00:35.617 --> 00:00:38.450
(baseball struck)

00:00:39.688 --> 00:00:42.358
(upbeat tuba music)

00:00:42.358 --> 00:00:45.169
Fighting within The Crips
is common and can often

00:00:45.169 --> 00:00:48.963
be very deadly. In 2016,
a group of neighborhoods

00:00:48.963 --> 00:00:51.797
in Los Angeles got together
to form a softball league

00:00:51.797 --> 00:00:54.020
as a way to heal the community.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.251
- I've been though a whole
decent a lot; I've been shot

00:00:56.251 --> 00:01:00.001
six times; I've been
around the dope dealing;

00:01:01.915 --> 00:01:05.318
I've done been around the
territory battles; and when I hit

00:01:05.318 --> 00:01:08.154
the streets, I learned the
street way of doing things, and

00:01:08.154 --> 00:01:10.337
I had to just sit up there
and, you know what I'm saying,

00:01:10.337 --> 00:01:12.584
ride the roller coaster.

00:01:12.584 --> 00:01:15.167
(upbeat music)

00:01:16.239 --> 00:01:20.625
- I met Terrell out here
playing softball in this league.

00:01:20.625 --> 00:01:22.526
And what I'm trying to do is
put something positive back

00:01:22.526 --> 00:01:23.611
into him.

00:01:23.611 --> 00:01:25.093
- It's still curving?

00:01:25.093 --> 00:01:26.850
- [Terrell Williams] A lil bit!

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.594
- I grew up with the negative,
and then I turned positive.

00:01:29.594 --> 00:01:30.427
You know what I'm saying,

00:01:30.427 --> 00:01:33.448
trying to be a better example to him.

00:01:33.448 --> 00:01:35.500
- I look at Tree as a brother.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.698
(baseball hits)

00:01:37.698 --> 00:01:38.906
(woos)

00:01:38.906 --> 00:01:43.360
We play Mondays, Wednesdays,
Fridays, Saturday together,

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.193
and sometimes Sundays.

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:49.318
What's up Tree, you run outta gas?

00:01:49.318 --> 00:01:50.936
(laughing)

00:01:50.936 --> 00:01:52.516
- Man, we even do a batting
practice at 3 o'clock

00:01:52.516 --> 00:01:54.390
in the morning; he can
call me at any time,

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.378
you know what I'm saying,
and I'm there for him.

00:01:56.378 --> 00:01:59.674
- He always say that, "I got
the talent, and you gotta

00:01:59.674 --> 00:02:02.347
"good future in front of
you, but you gunna have a lot

00:02:02.347 --> 00:02:05.803
"of people come at you, where
they trying to bring you down

00:02:05.803 --> 00:02:08.170
"and talk about you-you
just gotta leave that out

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.753
"the picture, and stay focused."

00:02:11.721 --> 00:02:13.914
- When I see something, that
you know what I'm saying,

00:02:13.914 --> 00:02:16.950
that I can help him with,
I don't hesitate at all.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.212
Because his happiness is my happiness.

00:02:19.212 --> 00:02:21.156
- I hope you ain't thinking
y'all gonna blow us out.

00:02:21.156 --> 00:02:24.064
- You'll understand by the time
we be raising that trophy up

00:02:24.064 --> 00:02:27.661
- We together right now.
But next week, I ain't gonna

00:02:27.661 --> 00:02:28.942
know who you are.

00:02:28.942 --> 00:02:29.775
- Oh, OK.

00:02:29.775 --> 00:02:32.207
(laughing)

00:02:32.207 --> 00:02:34.790
(upbeat music)

00:02:35.637 --> 00:02:38.172
- Despite being on rival
teams, Tree and Terrell have

00:02:38.172 --> 00:02:41.558
formed a family-like bond;
a league that started with

00:02:41.558 --> 00:02:43.668
four teams has quickly doubled to eight,

00:02:43.668 --> 00:02:46.423
and it's helping people come
together in ways that was once

00:02:46.423 --> 00:02:47.340
unheard of.

00:02:49.047 --> 00:02:51.127
- Everybody needs a friend
at the end of the day.

00:02:51.127 --> 00:02:53.275
And that's what I try to be
to Terrell-somebody that,

00:02:53.275 --> 00:02:55.496
you know what I'm
saying, he can depend on.

00:02:55.496 --> 00:02:57.523
- When we come together,
it's just a beautiful thing.

00:02:57.523 --> 00:03:00.802
There's no drama; you don't
see no police coming out,

00:03:00.802 --> 00:03:02.135
messing with us.

00:03:03.034 --> 00:03:05.045
- This is what our self-therapy
is: we come out here,

00:03:05.045 --> 00:03:07.724
and we just trying show love.

00:03:07.724 --> 00:03:09.974
(cheering)

